  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 4.2.0. Post-handlers are now uniformly outcome-aware (breaking): IPostHandlerAttribute.OnAfterHandle takes the request's RequestOutcome — the value the handler returned or the exception it threw — and runs on BOTH the success and exception paths (previously success only). This replaces 4.1.0's opt-in IPostHandlerOutcomeAware / OutcomeAwarePostHandlerAttribute (both removed): there is no longer an outcome-blind post-handler. Migration: add a RequestOutcome parameter to your OnAfterHandle implementations and read outcome.Result / outcome.Exception to classify on what happened.",
